<%- include('_pagehead', {
  eyebrow: 'Getting paid',
  heading: 'Card payments, into your account',
  lede: 'ConnectedWorkOS collects card payments through a payment processor you connect yourself — Stripe or Square, whichever you already use. Your money goes to your bank, we never hold it, and card numbers never touch our servers.'
}) %>

<!-- ══ Choose a processor ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band band--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band__head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">Two processors</p>
      <h2>Stripe or Square — bring the one you have</h2>
      <p>
        Most contractors already take cards somewhere. If that's Square — a reader in the
        truck, a register in the shop — connect it and your ConnectedWorkOS invoices land
        in the same account as your in-person sales, on the same payouts, in the same
        dashboard. If it's Stripe, or you have neither, Stripe is a free account you can
        open during setup.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Stripe</span>
        <h3>Online-first, free to open</h3>
        <p>The right choice if you don't take cards today, or already use Stripe. Setup includes Stripe's own onboarding — business details and a bank account — which takes about ten minutes once.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Square</span>
        <h3>Already on Square? Two minutes.</h3>
        <p>You sign in to the Square account you already have, approve the connection, and you're done — there's no second onboarding because Square already knows your business. Invoice payments show up next to your POS sales.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>One or the other, and you can switch.</strong> A business takes card payments
      through one processor at a time. Connect both if you like and choose which is live in
      Settings; payments already taken stay with the processor that took them.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ Setup ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band band--paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band__head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">Setting it up</p>
      <h2>Connecting, step by step</h2>
      <p>
        A one-time job. With Square it's a couple of minutes; with Stripe it's about ten,
        most of it Stripe's own onboarding rather than ours, so have your business details
        and a bank account to hand.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="steps__item">
        <span class="steps__no">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Open Settings → Payments</h3>
          <p>Inside ConnectedWorkOS. Two buttons: <em>Connect with Stripe</em> and <em>Connect with Square</em>. Pick the one you use.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="steps__item">
        <span class="steps__no">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Sign in to the processor</h3>
          <p>You're sent to Stripe or Square to sign in to your own account and approve the connection. If you already take card payments there, pick that account — you don't need a second one. New to Stripe? You create the account right there, and it's free to open.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="steps__item">
        <span class="steps__no">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>New Stripe account only: your business details</h3>
          <p>Stripe asks the questions a payment processor is legally required to ask: your business name and structure, an address, your EIN or SSN for a sole proprietor, and the bank account for payouts. This is between you and Stripe — we never see it. An existing Square or Stripe account has already answered these, so this step doesn't appear.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="steps__item">
        <span class="steps__no">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>You land back in ConnectedWorkOS, connected</h3>
          <p>That's it. Quotes can now take a deposit on acceptance, and invoices can be paid by card. Square businesses with more than one location pick which one payments are taken at.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout callout--warn">
      <strong>Until you connect an account, you cannot take card payments.</strong> Quoting,
      scheduling and invoicing all still work, but the pay page will tell your customer that
      payment isn't available. The setup checklist on your dashboard flags this for exactly
      that reason.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ Money flow ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="field">
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Where the money goes</p>
        <h2>It is your account, not ours</h2>
        <p>
          The connection is an authorisation — Stripe Connect, or Square's OAuth — that
          you grant and can revoke: you own the account, you agree to the processor's terms
          directly with them, and we're permitted to create charges and refunds on your
          behalf. We never take custody of your money, and we never hold your account keys.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow__head">Customer pays a deposit</div>
        <div class="flow__row"><span class="flow__label">Card charged</span><span class="flow__val flow__val--pay">$1,297.38</span></div>
        <div class="flow__arrow"><span>&#8595;</span> settles into</div>
        <div class="flow__head">Your Stripe or Square account</div>
        <div class="flow__row"><span class="flow__label">Less the processing fee</span><span class="flow__val">charged by the processor</span></div>
        <div class="flow__arrow"><span>&#8595;</span> pays out to</div>
        <div class="flow__head">Your bank account</div>
        <div class="flow__row"><span class="flow__label">On the processor's payout schedule</span><span class="flow__val">typically 1–2 business days</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<!-- ══ Fees ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band band--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band__head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">What it costs</p>
      <h2>Two separate bills, and we only send one</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">From us</span>
        <h3>Your subscription</h3>
        <p>A flat monthly or annual price for ConnectedWorkOS, billed as part of your Connected Home Ledger plan. It does not change with how much you invoice — we take no percentage of your jobs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">From Stripe or Square</span>
        <h3>Card processing fees</h3>
        <p>Your processor charges a per-transaction fee on each card payment and deducts it before payout. Those rates are theirs, they're published on Stripe's and Square's own pricing pages, and they can change — so we don't quote a number here that might be wrong by the time you read it. Square businesses pay the same online rate they already pay for invoices from Square itself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Nobody takes a cut of your revenue except the card networks.</strong> Some
      field-service tools charge you a percentage of every invoice on top of processing.
      We don't — you pay a subscription, your processor charges for moving money, and
      that's the whole list.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ Day to day ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band band--paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band__head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">Day to day</p>
      <h2>Once it's connected</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="cards cards--three">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Deposits</span>
        <h3>Collected on acceptance</h3>
        <p>Set a deposit percentage per quote. Accepting it raises the invoice and emails the pay link in the same action.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Balances</span>
        <h3>Billed when the job's done</h3>
        <p>Marking the work complete raises the remaining balance, net of the deposit. Send it, or let it sit until you're ready.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Refunds</span>
        <h3>Full or partial</h3>
        <p>Refund from the payment it belongs to, through whichever processor took it. The customer gets a receipt, and your books are adjusted so the income isn't overstated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Reconciliation</span>
        <h3>You can see the money</h3>
        <p>Every payment, with card brand and last four, a link to the processor's receipt, and a filterable sales journal you can export as CSV for your accountant.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Security</span>
        <h3>Card data never reaches us</h3>
        <p>The payment form is Stripe's or Square's, embedded in the page. Card numbers go from your customer to the processor directly — our servers never see or store them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Your customer</span>
        <h3>No account required</h3>
        <p>They click the link in your email, see the invoice, and pay. There's nothing to sign up for and nothing to install.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ Other processors ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band band--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band__head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">Other processors</p>
      <h2>Stripe and Square are what's supported today</h2>
      <p>
        Square was added because contractors asked for it. We're deliberately not listing
        processors we don't support yet — if the one you use matters to your decision,
        <a href="mailto:chris@connectedhomeoutfitters.com?subject=Payment%20processor">tell us which one</a>; that's
        the most useful signal for what we build next. In-person payments through a Square
        reader aren't part of ConnectedWorkOS yet; today the connection is for invoices paid
        online.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('_cta') %>
